---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Section } from "@/components/custom/section";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | ACOSA"
  description="Learn how ACOSA collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information."
>
  <Section>
    <article class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-8">
      <header class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h1 class="type-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">
          Effective date: 31.10.2026 · Last updated: 03.11.2026
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA respects your privacy and is committed to handling personal
          information responsibly.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          This Privacy Policy explains how ACOSA collects, uses, stores and
          protects personal information when you visit our website, enquire
          about accommodation, communicate with us or apply to list a property.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          We process personal information in accordance with applicable South
          African legislation, including the Protection of Personal Information
          Act 4 of 2013 (POPIA).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">2. Who we are</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA is a South African business-accommodation discovery platform
          connecting business travellers, corporate accommodation coordinators
          and other prospective guests with curated accommodation providers.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          For purposes of this Privacy Policy, ACOSA refers to:
        </p>
        <ul
          class="text-foreground/80 flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-6 leading-relaxed"
        >
          <li><strong>Business name:</strong> ACOSA (PTY) LTD</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Registered legal entity:</strong> 2025/703956/07 ACOSA (PTY) LTD
          </li>
          <li><strong>Country of operation:</strong> South Africa</li>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> info@acosa.co.za</li>
          <li><strong>Information Officer:</strong> Vanessa Joubert</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA operates as an online business-accommodation discovery platform.
          For privacy-related enquiries, please contact us using the email
          address provided above.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA is responsible for the personal information it processes for its
          own business purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">3. Information we collect</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Depending on how you interact with ACOSA, we may collect:
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Contact information</h3>
            <ul
              class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed"
            >
              <li>Name and surname</li>
              <li>Email address</li>
              <li>Telephone number</li>
              <li>Company or organisation name</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">
              Accommodation enquiry information
            </h3>
            <ul
              class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed"
            >
              <li>Preferred accommodation location</li>
              <li>Intended travel dates</li>
              <li>Number of travellers or rooms required</li>
              <li>Accommodation preferences and requirements</li>
              <li>Other information you voluntarily provide</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Property listing information</h3>
            <ul
              class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed"
            >
              <li>Property and establishment details</li>
              <li>Owner or representative contact information</li>
              <li>Property address and location</li>
              <li>Accommodation descriptions, photographs and amenities</li>
              <li>Website and social media details</li>
              <li>Information required to review or administer a listing</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Website usage information</h3>
            <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
              Where enabled, website analytics may record information such as
              pages visited, approximate traffic sources, device or browser
              information, and interactions with property listings.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          We ask visitors not to provide unnecessary sensitive personal
          information when submitting enquiries.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">4. How we use your information</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA processes personal information for legitimate business purposes,
          including:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>Responding to enquiries.</li>
          <li>Helping visitors identify relevant accommodation options.</li>
          <li>Communicating with accommodation providers.</li>
          <li>Reviewing property listing applications.</li>
          <li>Creating and maintaining approved property profiles.</li>
          <li>Administering business relationships and payments.</li>
          <li>Improving website functionality and visitor experience.</li>
          <li>Measuring property listing visibility and engagement.</li>
          <li>Maintaining appropriate business and legal records.</li>
          <li>Complying with applicable legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          We process personal information only where there is an appropriate
          lawful basis, including consent where required, contractual necessity,
          compliance with legal obligations or other grounds permitted by POPIA.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">5. Is providing information compulsory?</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Providing information through an accommodation enquiry or property
          listing request is generally voluntary.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          However, certain information may be necessary for ACOSA to respond
          meaningfully, assess a property application or administer an agreed
          service.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          If essential information is not supplied, we may be unable to process
          the relevant request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">6. Sharing information</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may share relevant information with:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            Accommodation providers when necessary to facilitate an enquiry.
          </li>
          <li>
            Authorised employees or service providers assisting with website
            operations.
          </li>
          <li>
            Technology providers supporting email, hosting, communications and
            analytics.
          </li>
          <li>Professional advisers where reasonably necessary.</li>
          <li>
            Regulatory or legal authorities where disclosure is required by law.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          We do not sell personal information to third parties.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Information is shared only where appropriate for the relevant purpose
          and subject to applicable legal requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">7. Accommodation enquiries</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          When you enquire about accommodation, ACOSA may use the information
          supplied to identify suitable properties or facilitate communication
          with accommodation providers.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Where your enquiry is forwarded to a property, that provider may
          process your information under its own privacy practices.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          We encourage visitors to review the relevant provider's privacy
          information before supplying additional personal details or completing
          a reservation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">8. Property listings and performance reporting</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may collect website activity information relating to individual
          property listings.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Where technically available, this may include property profile views
          and interactions with contact buttons or external links.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          This information may be used to prepare performance snapshots for the
          relevant property owner or authorised representative.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Such reporting is intended to measure listing exposure and engagement.
          It does not necessarily establish that an enquiry, reservation or
          transaction was completed.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA will take reasonable steps to ensure that reporting does not
          unnecessarily disclose identifiable visitor information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">9. Cookies and website analytics</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Our website may use cookies or similar technologies to support
          functionality, understand website usage and improve performance.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          The technologies used, and whether they require consent, depend on the
          services enabled on the website.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          <strong>Website technologies currently used:</strong> [Insert confirmed
          hosting, analytics and cookie technologies.]
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Where required by applicable law, visitors will be given appropriate
          information and choices regarding non-essential tracking.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          You may also manage certain cookies through your browser settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">10. Communication and marketing</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may contact you in response to an enquiry, property application
          or existing business relationship.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          We will not treat an accommodation enquiry as automatic permission to
          send unrelated promotional communications.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Where direct marketing requires consent or another lawful basis, ACOSA
          will comply with the applicable requirements.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Recipients of marketing communications will be provided with an
          appropriate method of opting out.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">11. Storage and security</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA takes reasonable technical and organisational measures to
          protect personal information against unauthorised access, loss,
          misuse, alteration or disclosure.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          However, no electronic communication or storage system can be
          guaranteed to be completely secure.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Personal information is retained only for as long as reasonably
          necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, subject to
          applicable legal, contractual and recordkeeping obligations.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          When information is no longer required, ACOSA will take appropriate
          steps to delete, destroy or de-identify it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">12. International processing</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Some technology service providers used by ACOSA may store or process
          information outside South Africa.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Where this occurs, ACOSA will take reasonable steps to ensure that the
          transfer complies with applicable POPIA requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">13. Your privacy rights</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Subject to applicable law, you may request:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            Confirmation of whether ACOSA holds personal information about you.
          </li>
          <li>Access to personal information held about you.</li>
          <li>Correction or updating of inaccurate information.</li>
          <li>Deletion of information where legally appropriate.</li>
          <li>
            Information about the processing of your personal information.
          </li>
          <li>Withdrawal of consent where processing depends on consent.</li>
          <li>An objection to processing where permitted by law.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Requests may be directed to:
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          <strong>Privacy enquiries:</strong>
          <a
            class="underline underline-offset-4"
            href="mailto:info@acosa.co.za"
          >
            info@acosa.co.za
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          We may need to verify your identity before processing certain
          requests.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          You may also lodge a complaint with the South African Information
          Regulator.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">14. Third-party websites</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          The ACOSA website may contain links to accommodation providers, maps,
          messaging services and other external websites.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA does not control the privacy practices of these third parties.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Visitors should review the relevant third-party privacy policies when
          leaving our website.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">15. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in its
          services, technology or legal obligations.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          The latest version will be published on this website with an updated
          revision date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">16. Contact us</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          For questions about this Privacy Policy or the processing of your
          personal information, contact:
        </p>
        <address
          class="text-foreground/80 flex flex-col gap-1 leading-relaxed not-italic"
        >
          <strong>ACOSA (PTY) LTD</strong>
          <span>Email: info@acosa.co.za</span>
          <span>Information Officer: Vanessa Joubert</span>
          <span>
            ACOSA operates as an online business-accommodation discovery
            platform. For privacy-related enquiries, please contact us using the
            email address provided above.
          </span>
        </address>
      </section>
    </article>
  </Section>
</Layout>
